# Rule: excessive_file_read
# Category: Data Exfiltration
# Severity: medium
# Attack Class: exfiltration
#
# Detects agents reading an abnormally high number of UNIQUE files in a short
# window. May indicate an agent attempting to enumerate and exfiltrate file
# contents.
#
# Threshold: more than 50 unique filenames in 60 seconds.
# Uses count_distinct() to count unique files, not total read events.
# This catches bulk file scanning while allowing repeated reads of the same file.

event.type == "FILE_READ" AND count_distinct("FILE_READ", "raw_data.filename", "60s") > 50
